# Metrics

This app exposes framework-owned metrics through `github.com/goforj/metrics`.

Current baseline coverage includes:

- total HTTP requests
- in-flight HTTP requests
- 4xx response count
- 5xx response count
- HTTP request duration histogram
- cache operation counters by cache, driver, operation, status, and hit result
- cache operation latency histogram by cache, driver, and operation
- storage operation counters by disk, driver, operation, and status
- storage operation latency histogram by disk, driver, and operation
- event publish counters by bus, driver, topic, and status
- event publish latency histogram by bus, driver, and topic
{{- if .Components.Mail }}
- mail send counters by mailer, driver, and status
- mail send latency histogram by mailer and driver
{{- end }}
{{- if .Components.Jobs }}
- queue enqueue / scheduled / processed / failed / retried / archived counters
- queue in-flight job gauge by queue
- queue processing duration histogram by queue
{{- end }}
{{- if .Components.Scheduler }}
- scheduler success / failure / skip counters
- scheduler job outcome counters by schedule name
- scheduler job duration histogram by schedule name
{{- end }}
{{- if .Components.HasDatabase }}
- database statement counters by connection, driver, operation, and status
- database statement latency histogram by connection, driver, and operation
{{- end }}

## Endpoints

{{- if or .Components.WebAPI .Components.WebUI }}
- API metrics: `http://localhost:9100/metrics`
{{- end }}
{{- if .Components.Jobs }}
- Jobs metrics: `http://localhost:9101/metrics`
{{- end }}
{{- if .Components.Scheduler }}
- Scheduler metrics: `http://localhost:9102/metrics`
{{- end }}
{{- if .Components.WebAPI }}
- App HTTP route: `GET /metrics`
  - Prometheus text exposition
  - served without auth by default
{{- end }}

## Notes

- Metrics are registered during app startup through DI.
- Runtime process metrics are exposed through lightweight dedicated `net/http` listeners.
- Export uses snapshot-based Prometheus encoding.
- Additional app-defined metrics can be registered through the shared metrics manager.
{{- if .Components.Observability }}
- The local observability stack is documented in `internal/observability/README.md`.
{{- end }}
